course: dictionary
lesson: 7184
title: Giving things a human touch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To personify something means to describe a thing, an animal or an idea as if it were a person, with human feelings or actions. «The wind howled angrily» gives the wind an angry voice, even though wind cannot really feel anything.
explain: Writers do this to make a picture come alive. «The sun smiled down» makes the sun sound warm and friendly, not just bright. «The trees whispered» gives the trees a voice, so you can almost hear them.
explain: Personify has a second meaning too. «She personifies kindness» means she is the best example of kindness, so kindness seems to live in her. Check your meaning by swapping in "is a perfect example of" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Personify is a verb: personify, personifies, personified, personifying.
fact: «Personify» means to describe a thing, animal or idea as if it were a person.
fact: Personification is a figure of speech, a way of using words to make writing more vivid.
fact: Good personification often uses one or two human actions, such as watching or whispering.
fact: «Personifies» can also mean being a perfect example of a quality: «She personifies kindness.»
exercise: «The sun smiled down on the fields.» Which words show personification? | *The sun smiled | The sun is very hot | The fields are wide | The sun is yellow
exercise: «The trees whispered secrets to each other.» Which thing is given a human action? | The secrets | Nothing, it is a plain description | Each other | *The trees
exercise: Nadia says «She personifies patience» means she is always tired. What does it really mean? | She is always in a hurry | *She is the best example of being patient | She never speaks | She is very tall
test: «The moon watched us from the sky.» Which word gives the moon a human action? | Us | Sky | Moon | *Watched
test: «He personifies courage.» What does this sentence mean? | He has a pet horse | He is afraid of heights | *He is the best example of courage | He is very loud
exam: Which sentence uses personification? | The clock is on the wall | The clock has hands | *The clock ticked its way through the long night | The clock is round
